; Regression test for GitHub issue #3314: postings to [bracketed] accounts
; balance only against one another, never against the real postings of
; their transaction (#2105).  Ledger 3.4 summed the two groups together,
; so it accepted both of these transactions, and their real postings
; did not balance.  An elided posting balances only its own group, and
; the error names the group whose postings leave a remainder.

2018-10-22 Test
    Assets:Test                      10.00 EUR
    [Assets:Bank]

2020-05-30 * Virtual
    [Expenses:Virtual]                  2.00 EUR
    Expenses:Food
    Assets:Cash                       -10.00 EUR

test bal -> 2
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 10:
While balancing transaction from "$FILE", lines 8-10:
> 2018-10-22 Test
>     Assets:Test                      10.00 EUR
>     [Assets:Bank]
Unbalanced remainder of real postings is:
           10.00 EUR
Amount to balance against:
           10.00 EUR
Error: Transaction does not balance
While parsing file "$FILE", line 15:
While balancing transaction from "$FILE", lines 12-15:
> 2020-05-30 * Virtual
>     [Expenses:Virtual]                  2.00 EUR
>     Expenses:Food
>     Assets:Cash                       -10.00 EUR
Unbalanced remainder of balanced virtual postings is:
            2.00 EUR
Amount to balance against:
            2.00 EUR
Error: Transaction does not balance
end test
